Annex III indicates that the economic analysis conducted by 2004 should support the assessment of the most cost-effective combination of measures to be included in the Programme of Measures (Article 11). Such cost-effectiveness analysis requires an identification of environmental objectives for each water body, an assessment of possible measures to meet these objectives, an estimate of their costs and of their impact on the status of water bodies.

